Chapter: Gaze
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceMath
  cites Safari chapter Num
  cites Safari chapter Trig
  cites Safari chapter Pose
  cites Safari chapter World

 The distracted rider: his head swivels toward the roadside pigs and drifts back
 to the road, and his focus narrows while he gawks.

 A port of wasm/gaze.zig.

 BOTH OUTPUTS ARE VIEW-ONLY except one. `gaze-yaw` is an extra camera yaw and
 `focus` feeds the focal pull-in; neither moves the bike. The single reach into
 the motion is `pig-gaze-brake`, which the rider folds into its min-of-brakes --
 and that is the whole of the distraction's cost in metres.

 It takes the RiderState from `Safari chapter Pose` rather than from Rider,
 because the zig has rider.zig and gaze.zig importing each other and Codex cites
 cannot. See Pose for why the record is the right place to cut it.

 We say:

Section: Thresholds

  gaze-look-dist : Real
  gaze-look-dist = 150.0

 The gaze peaks here; once the pig swings this far off his heading he looks back.

  gaze-release-angle : Real
  gaze-release-angle = 35.0 * deg

 The most his head turns TOWARD the pig in one frame -- a gentle swivel -- against
 the slow, unhurried drift BACK to the road.

  gaze-swivel-rate : Real
  gaze-swivel-rate = 4.0 * deg

  gaze-return-rate : Real
  gaze-return-rate = 0.2 * deg

 Near straight the return step shrinks to this fraction of the remaining angle, so
 it decelerates in; below the snap angle the last sliver goes to zero, which keeps
 the focus trigger exact.

  gaze-return-ease : Real
  gaze-return-ease = 0.05

  gaze-return-snap : Real
  gaze-return-snap = 0.02 * deg

  focus-decay : Real
  focus-decay = 0.0012

 The slow gawk speed he eases to and then HOLDS for the rest of the segment, and
 how far before the pig he finishes slowing.

  pig-gaze-speed : Real
  pig-gaze-speed = 0.20

  pig-gaze-settle-dist : Real
  pig-gaze-settle-dist = 25.0

 Pointed more than this off the lane means mid-corner, and his eyes snap back to
 the road.

  eyes-on-road-yaw : Real
  eyes-on-road-yaw = 6.0 * deg

Section: Focus

  smoothstep : Real -> Real
  smoothstep (t) = t * t * (3.0 - 2.0 * t)

 state.focus is a LINEAR progress; this smoothsteps it so the narrow and the
 re-widen ease gently in and out.

  gaze-focus : Real -> Real
  gaze-focus (f) = smoothstep f

Section: Looking

 Is the designated pig still AHEAD and inside the looking window: a distraction
 leg, eyes not committed to a corner, the pig within the look distance, and not
 yet swung past the release angle off his heading.

 The zig returns an optional distance. Codex has no null, so the two answers are a
 record -- `looking` says whether there is any pig interest at all, and every
 caller checks it before reading `dist`.

  PigLook = record {
    looking : Boolean,
    dist : Real
  }

  no-look : PigLook
  no-look = PigLook { looking = False, dist = 0.0 }

  pig-ahead : RiderState, Segment -> PigLook
  pig-ahead (state) (seg) =
    if seg.pigs-distract == False then no-look
    else if real-abs state.yaw > eyes-on-road-yaw then no-look
    else pig-ahead-near state seg

  pig-ahead-near : RiderState, Segment -> PigLook
  pig-ahead-near (state) (seg) =
    let pig = gaze-pig seg.length (seg.width / 2.0)
    in let dist = pig.along - state.along
    in if dist > gaze-look-dist then no-look
    else pig-ahead-bearing state pig dist

  pig-ahead-bearing : RiderState, Critter, Real -> PigLook
  pig-ahead-bearing (state) (pig) (dist) =
    let bearing = r-atan2 (pig.across - state.across) dist - state.yaw
    in if real-abs bearing >= gaze-release-angle then no-look
       else PigLook { looking = True, dist = dist }

 Where he WANTS to look this frame: the bearing to the designated pig relative to
 his heading, or zero when he has no pig interest. A BEARING, not a fixed angle,
 so his gaze tracks the pig as he creeps past it.

  desired-gaze : RiderState, Segment -> Real
  desired-gaze (state) (seg) =
    if (pig-ahead state seg).looking == False then 0.0
    else desired-gaze-at state (gaze-pig seg.length (seg.width / 2.0))

  desired-gaze-at : RiderState, Critter -> Real
  desired-gaze-at (state) (pig) =
    r-atan2 (pig.across - state.across) (pig.along - state.along) - state.yaw

Section: The Gaze Step

 Run AFTER the bike has moved: swivel his head one frame toward where he wants to
 look. Toward the pig is a gentle fixed-rate swivel; the drift back to the road
 lingers, then decelerates into straight, snapping the last sliver to zero.

 The `want /= 0` test is a Real comparison the zig writes as `want != 0`, which is
 bitwise, so it is ~0 here and not ~. desired-gaze returns a LITERAL zero when
 there is no interest, so the two answers really are exactly zero or not, and a
 4-ULP tolerance would swallow a genuinely tiny bearing and send his eyes back to
 the road a frame early.

  next-gaze-yaw : RiderState, Real -> Real
  next-gaze-yaw (state) (want) =
    if (want ~0 0.0) == False then state.gaze-yaw + real-max (0.0 - gaze-swivel-rate) (real-min gaze-swivel-rate (want - state.gaze-yaw))
    else if real-abs state.gaze-yaw <= gaze-return-snap then 0.0
    else state.gaze-yaw - r-sign state.gaze-yaw * real-min gaze-return-rate (real-abs state.gaze-yaw * gaze-return-ease)

 While his head is turned the focus rises with the turn and HOLDS its peak; it
 eases out only once he is fully straightened.

  next-focus : RiderState, Real -> Real
  next-focus (state) (gaze-yaw) =
    if gaze-yaw ~0 0.0 then real-max 0.0 (state.focus - focus-decay)
    else real-max state.focus (real-min (real-abs gaze-yaw / gaze-release-angle) 1.0)

  next-rider-gaze : RiderState, List Segment -> RiderState
  next-rider-gaze (state) (segs) =
    let want = desired-gaze state (list-at segs state.segment)
    in let gy = next-gaze-yaw state want
    in RiderState { segment = state.segment, along = state.along, across = state.across, yaw = state.yaw, v = state.v, tilt = state.tilt, heading = state.heading, gaze-yaw = gy, focus = next-focus state gy }

Section: The Gawk

 Once he has NOTICED the pigs he is committed to the slow gawk for the REST of the
 segment: sticky and purely positional, and the crossing resets him next segment.
 Distinct from pig-ahead, which is the HEAD turn and ends once the pig is beside
 him; this is the MOTION hold, so it ignores the eyes-on-road gate and persists
 into the turn.

  gawk-engaged : RiderState, Segment -> Boolean
  gawk-engaged (state) (seg) =
    if seg.pigs-distract == False then False
    else state.along >= (gaze-pig seg.length (seg.width / 2.0)).along - gaze-look-dist

 THE GAWK BRAKE, which the rider folds into its min-of-brakes. Not engaged until
 he has noticed the pigs; from then on he eases toward the gawk speed by the same
 kinematic law the corner brake uses, timed to settle a little before the pig so
 he creeps PAST it at that speed, and then holds.

 `engaged` is the optional the zig returns: nothing at all until he notices.

  GazeBrake = record {
    engaged : Boolean,
    accel : Real
  }

  pig-gaze-brake : RiderState, Segment -> GazeBrake
  pig-gaze-brake (state) (seg) =
    if gawk-engaged state seg == False then GazeBrake { engaged = False, accel = 0.0 }
    else if state.v <= pig-gaze-speed then GazeBrake { engaged = True, accel = 0.0 }
    else pig-gaze-brake-easing state seg

  pig-gaze-brake-easing : RiderState, Segment -> GazeBrake
  pig-gaze-brake-easing (state) (seg) =
    let d = (gaze-pig seg.length (seg.width / 2.0)).along - state.along - pig-gaze-settle-dist
    in GazeBrake { engaged = True, accel = (pig-gaze-speed * pig-gaze-speed - state.v * state.v) / (2.0 * real-max d 1.0) }
